-### SpatialHash3D
-SpatialHash3D is a spatial index structure that uses a uniform 3D hash grid to enable efficient nearest-neighbor and radius-based queries for static datasets, providing O(1) cell lookup [S1]. It differs from its siblings, such as the [Voxel World Data Structure](1101-voxel-world-data-structure.md) which manages dynamic voxel worlds, and [Hash Grid Loss](2093-hash-grid-loss.md) which focuses on optimization objectives, by prioritizing predictable performance and straightforward implementation for static interpolation tasks [S1]. It builds on the general hashing principles of [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md) but applies them specifically to uniform 3D spatial partitioning for query acceleration.
